    "physical_description": "This silk temple hanging has been elaborately decorated using weft ikat technique; it has been woven in twill weave and depicts scenes from life of the Buddha.",
    "summary": "Khmer weavers in Cambodia use weft ikat technique to decorate lustruous temple hangings with Buddhist imagery. The clarity of the pictorial scenes depicting the Life of Buddha on this example demonstrates the maker's technical virtuosity in dyeing and weaving the weft threads. The use of twill weave heightens the brilliance of the cloth's surface.",
